Subject: [PATCH 2/2] jails: Keep lab-claude's .claude.json in the claude dir
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: lnststtmqlmokupuvptzssstyntxyzyk

Claude Code keeps its global config, ~/.claude.json, beside the
claude dir rather than in it, so the persistent claude dir mount does
not cover it. Onboarding state, the account, and per-project trust
are lost on every rebuild.

Claude Code resolves the config as $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.claude.json
when that variable is set, and keeps everything else it would put in
~/.claude in the same directory. Setting it to ~/.claude in the login
environment moves the config into the mounted dir and leaves all
other paths where they were. A config already at ~/.claude.json is
not migrated; move it into ~/.claude once.
---
change-id: lnststtmqlmokupuvptzssstyntxyzyk

 jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf b/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf
index f3a0497..d0ceead 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.login_conf
@@ -8,12 +8,18 @@
 # https://bugs.freebsd.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=298878
 # https://bugs.freebsd.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=299200
 #
+# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR keeps .claude.json inside ~/.claude, which is
+# mounted from the host, so the config persists with the rest of
+# Claude's state.  It is not in claude-jail.sh; only this jail mounts
+# the claude dir.
+#
 # getcap(3) does not allow comments inside a record, so they all
 # live up here.
 
 me:\
 	:setenv=\
 	BUN_JSC_useConcurrentGC=0,\
+	CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/claude/.claude,\
 	CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ALTERNATE_SCREEN=1,\
 	CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AGENT_VIEW=1,\
 	CLAUDE_AX_SCREEN_READER=1,\
